From: OWzx <owzx@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0016] perf(tsp): bound crossing-scan iterations (v2.5.0 rebase)

perf(tsp): bound crossing-scan iterations (v2.5.0 rebase)
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/GCode/OrderingStrategies.cpp b/src/libslic3r/GCode/OrderingStrategies.cpp
index 4ac7ce6c..70b17ae4 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/GCode/OrderingStrategies.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/GCode/OrderingStrategies.cpp
@@ -195,7 +195,15 @@ bool tsp_remove_crossings(std::vector<size_t>& path, const Points& centers)
 
     // Process crossings one at a time: find first, reverse it, restart scan.
     // Cap iterations to prevent infinite loops on collinear/overlapping segments.
-    const int max_iters = static_cast<int>(pn * pn);
+    // owzx-fix (TSP-CAP): each iteration is an O(pn^2) crossing scan, so the
+    // upstream pn*pn cap is O(pn^4) work -- degenerate inputs spun for hours
+    // (2583-point multicolor path). Keep the cap while total scan work stays
+    // under ~5e7 pair checks; beyond that allow at least 128 reversals. Paths
+    // up to ~84 points are bit-identical to upstream.
+    const long long pn2 = static_cast<long long>(pn) * static_cast<long long>(pn);
+    const long long budget =
+        std::max<long long>(128, 50000000LL / std::max<long long>(pn2, 1));
+    const int max_iters = static_cast<int>(std::min<long long>(pn2, budget));
     bool improved = false;
     // Reversing between two segments that only touch or overlap along a line need not remove the intersection, so on
     // islands laid out on a regular grid (a tiled texture, an array of parts) the loop can cycle through the same
